.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ── Agent-tooling artifacts (machine-local; never commit) ─────
# The skills-manager extension writes telemetry and per-vendor config mirrors
# into the repo. Two reasons none of it belongs here:
#   1. mcp-usage.jsonl records absolute local paths, session IDs, and full
#      bash command strings — this repo is public.
#   2. The learning/ stores are per-machine state; committing them would make
#      every clone inherit one developer's cost and adoption history.
# Globbed rather than path-listed because the hooks resolve from cwd, not the
# repo root — running a command in ts/ or npm/ grows another copy.
**/.claude/learning/
**/.claude/mcp-usage.jsonl

# Same extension, re-emitting the local .claude/skills/ set per agent vendor.
# .claude/skills/ is itself untracked, so these mirrors document tooling no
# contributor has — committing them would be pure drift.
# Subpaths, not the whole dir: `.cursor/mcp.json` is tracked, shared config.
.cursor/hooks.json
.cursor/learning/
.cursor/skills/
.kiro/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/instructions/
.github/hooks/

# harness CLI machine identity — regenerated per install
**/.harness/.install-id
**/.harness/.telemetry-notice-shown

# Proprietary denylist for the company-leak guard (kept local; CI uses a secret)
.proprietary-denylist

# Downloaded native binaries (placed by npm postinstall)
npm/bin/canary
npm/bin/canary.exe

# Local turbo→ruff lint bridge (pairs with gitignored root package.json; see issue #253)
/turbo.json
